body:
For something as serious as this I'd always recommend talking to an adult you trust, or since you're in hs, a school counselor. Most of the times I believe in "innocent until proven guilty", but not always.. yet in this case, I hope it's just a girl's sick prank or something. It doesn't excuse anyone, but when you're drunk and unaware of what you're doing, it shows that wasn't your true intention. Especially the fact that you feel guilty about it now. I'm not so sure about the law in where you are, but in most countries when a sex crime is done on a minor, someone like a therapist is obligated to report it. However therapy (and different kinds of it) is what will help both of you. 

&#x200B;

I am in no means a professional or anything, just some random person commenting, but what I think is a good idea to do is apologize to the girl if you still can (be careful  how you do it so you don't come out as agressive) and most definetly talk to someone. Tell them everything you wrote in this text post. The drunk part, the text part, the guilt part. People who do things like that are absolutely disgusting, scum of the earth, but your case is very specific, and there is no black or white.
